{"schema_version":"1.9.0","id":"OESA-2026-3151","published":"2026-07-24T11:12:01Z","modified":"2026-08-18T01:21:25.255262112Z","upstream":["CVE-2026-14474"],"summary":"sssd security update","details":"Provides a set of daemons to manage access to remote directories and authentication mechanisms. It provides an NSS and PAM interface toward the system and a pluggable back end system to connect to multiple different account sources. It is also the basis to provide client auditing and policy services for projects like FreeIPA.\r\n\r\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\nA flaw was found in SSSD&apos;s LDAP sudo provider. When the ldap_sudo_search_base option is not explicitly configured, SSSD searches the entire LDAP directory tree for sudoRole objects. An authenticated attacker with write access to any subtree can inject a sudoRole object granting root-level sudo privileges on all SSSD-enrolled hosts.(CVE-2026-14474)","affected":[{"package":{"name":"sssd","ecosystem":"openEuler:24.03-LTS-SP4","purl":"pkg:rpm/openEuler/sssd&distro=openEuler-24.03-LTS-SP4"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"2.9.4-22.oe2403sp4"}]}],"ecosystem_specific":{"aarch64":["libipa_hbac-2.9.4-22.oe2403sp4.aarch64.rpm","libipa_hbac-devel-2.9.4-22.oe2403sp4.aarch64.rpm","libsss_autofs-2.9.4-22.oe2403sp4.aarch64.rpm","libsss_certmap-2.9.4-22.oe2403sp4.aarch64.rpm","libsss_certmap-devel-2.9.4-22.oe2403sp4.aarch64.rpm","libsss_idmap-2.9.4-22.oe2403sp4.aarch64.rpm","libsss_idmap-devel-2.9.4-22.oe2403sp4.aarch64.rpm","libsss_nss_idmap-2.9.4-22.oe2403sp4.aarch64.rpm","libsss_nss_idmap-devel-2.9.4-22.oe2403sp4.aarch64.rpm","libsss_sudo-2.9.4-22.oe2403sp4.aarch64.rpm","python3-libipa_hbac-2.9.4-22.oe2403sp4.aarch64.rpm","python3-libsss_nss_idmap-2.9.4-22.oe2403sp4.aarch64.rpm","python3-sss-2.9.4-22.oe2403sp4.aarch64.rpm","python3-sss-murmur-2.9.4-22.oe2403sp4.aarch64.rpm","sssd-2.9.4-22.oe2403sp4.aarch64.rpm","sssd-ad-2.9.4-22.oe2403sp4.aarch64.rpm","sssd-client-2.9.4-22.oe2403sp4.aarch64.